# expected: {"a":1.5} — docs (reference-language.md, Preference section):
#           "A kind peer the default already satisfies leaves the
#           preference standing (`a:*1.5 & float` ... are both 1.5)",
#           and that holds at rank 1: a:*1.5 & float -> 1.5
# actual: rank >= 2 is swallowed by ANY conjunct: a:**1.5 & float ->
#         [aontu/mapval_no_gen] exit 1 (canon shows the default dropped);
#         likewise b below: **2|integer met by a bare `integer` statement
#         loses the default (canon {"b":integer}), while *2|integer keeps it
a: **1.5 & float
b: **2 | integer
b: integer
